    "result_text": "The full suite builds green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the email-uniqueness rule for `POST /api/owners`, rejecting a new owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner with HTTP 409, following the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n- **`EnsureUniqueEmail.java`** \u2014 new pipeline step. Reads the already-normalized (lower-cased) email from the `OwnerFieldsDto` variable; email is optional so a null/blank value is skipped; otherwise compares against every existing owner's lower-cased email and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a match.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds 409 via `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the telephone handler.\n- **escalation YAML** \u2014 `...escalation.DuplicateEmailException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted `ensureUniqueEmail` right after `normalizeEmail` (so it sees the lower-cased value) and before `ensureUniqueTelephone`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
